    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Dear students,"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Interesting after-school activities are important for the development of each one of you. These activities are important because they give you the chance to express yourselves "
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "creatively",
              "ref": "v-creatively"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ". For this reason, the school has "
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "organized",
              "ref": "v-organize"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " an English speech contest for students. The competition will be held at the school "
            },
            {
              "t": "gloss",
              "v": "auditorium",
              "zh": "礼堂"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " on April 25, 2026. All students can "
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "participate in",
              "ref": "v-participate-in"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " it."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "Contestants",
              "ref": "v-contestant"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " will be divided into three groups: Grade One students, Grade Two students and Grade Three students. The contest will have two "
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "phases",
              "ref": "v-phase"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ": the initial and the final. In the initial phase, contestants are free to choose their topics. English teachers will be invited to be the judges. The top five contestants in each group will go through to the final. In the final, each contestant will be given a topic. The top three will be the final winners. They will be awarded prizes by the "
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "principal",
              "ref": "v-principal"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " of our school."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "If you are interested, please come to the Student Union Office in Room 203 of Teaching Building Ⅱ. For more information, please call Mr. Zhang at 88413677-6203."
            }
          ]
        ],
        "signature": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Student Union"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
